libmdnsd: ship a pkg-config file

The library installs a header directory and a versioned .so but no .pc, so
every consumer has to hard-code -lmdnsd and guess at the include path.
Buildroot packages that link it would each carry that knowledge separately,
which is exactly what pkg-config exists to stop.

Cflags is -I${includedir} rather than ${includedir}/libmdnsd, because the
headers are installed with nobase_ and are meant to be reached as
<libmdnsd/mdnsd.h>.

pkgconfigdir is spelled out instead of using PKG_INSTALLDIR: the macro comes
from pkg.m4, and the package should not gain a build-time dependency on
pkg-config's macros just to name a directory every autotools project already
knows.

Upstream: not submitted.
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 AC_CONFIG_SRCDIR(src/mdnsd.c)
 AC_CONFIG_HEADERS(config.h)
 AC_CONFIG_FILES([Makefile mdnsd.service
+		 libmdnsd.pc
 		 examples/Makefile
 		 libmdnsd/Makefile
 		 man/Makefile
--- a/Makefile.am
+++ b/Makefile.am
@@ -5,6 +5,9 @@
 doc_DATA                = README.md ChangeLog.md LICENSE
 EXTRA_DIST              = README.md ChangeLog.md LICENSE
 
+pkgconfigdir            = $(libdir)/pkgconfig
+pkgconfig_DATA          = libmdnsd.pc
+
 if HAVE_SYSTEMD
 systemd_DATA            = mdnsd.service
 endif
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libmdnsd.pc.in
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+prefix=@prefix@
+exec_prefix=@exec_prefix@
+libdir=@libdir@
+includedir=@includedir@
+
+Name: libmdnsd
+Description: Embeddable mDNS-SD (multicast DNS service discovery) library
+URL: https://github.com/troglobit/mdnsd
+Version: @PACKAGE_VERSION@
+Libs: -L${libdir} -lmdnsd
+Cflags: -I${includedir}
